course: dictionary
lesson: 854
title: Betting: risking money on a guess
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Betting means risking money on what will happen, such as who will win a race, in the hope of winning more money. The word has a second, everyday use too: «I'm betting you'll like it» means «I'm sure you'll like it», because betting is the -ing form of the verb bet. Look for clues to see which meaning is meant. Is money involved, or is someone just sure about something?
explain: Here is a sentence with clues: «In street betting games with cups and a ball, the winners are often the trickster's helpers, and ordinary players lose.» The clues are trickster, helpers and lose. The players are risking money on a guess, and the game is set up so that the ordinary player usually loses.
explain: Maths explains why. Betting usually loses money over time, because the odds are set so the bookmaker wins. Even a small bet between friends makes nothing overall: if one wins £1, the other loses £1, and «rows often follow».
fact: Betting means risking money on what will happen, in the hope of winning more money.
fact: In everyday speech, «I'm betting» means «I think» or «I'm sure».
fact: Betting usually loses money in the long run, because the odds are set so the bookmaker wins.
fact: «When the fun stops, stop» is a warning that betting adverts must include, because gambling can become an addiction.
fact: Betting for money is against the law for children.
exercise: «I'm betting you'll like it.» What does «I'm betting» mean here? | *I'm sure you'll like it | I'm risking money that you'll like it | I'm running a race to find out | I'm hoping you will not like it
exercise: In a street game with cups and a ball, who often wins? | *The trickster's helpers | Ordinary players who guess well | Children with the most pocket money | Everyone, equally
exercise: Why do many families have a "no betting for money" rule for kids? | Because it makes money for the family | Because betting is a fun game for everyone | *Because bets between friends can end in rows and losses | Because betting makes you taller
test: What does betting mean in its first meaning? | *Risking money on what will happen, hoping to win more | Playing a board game | Reading a report about a race | Giving someone a gift
test: Why does betting usually lose money over time? | Because the bookmaker has no money to pay out | *Because the odds are set so the bookmaker wins | Because the winnings are hidden from players | Because people are unlucky every day
exam: Which is the best reason to say betting is a risky habit for a child to start? | *Because it can become a harmful habit, and it is against the law for children | Because it makes you win money every time | Because it is always fair and safe | Because the odds are equal for everyone
